From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Large_language_model, it is stated that LLMs are a type of neural network trained on a vast amount of text for natural language processing tasks, especially language generation. They can generate, summarize, translate, and parse text in many contexts and are a foundational technology behind modern chatbots.

From https://www.ibm.com/topics/artificial-intelligence, it is mentioned that large language models (LLMs) are a type of foundation model, which serves as the basis for multiple different types of generative AI applications, specifically for text generation applications.

Comparing the two sources, it can be seen that both describe LLMs as a key component of AI, particularly in natural language processing and generation tasks. The Wikipedia source provides more detailed information on the capabilities and applications of LLMs, while the IBM source highlights their role as a foundation model for generative AI applications.

There is no contradiction between the sources, and they both suggest that LLMs are a crucial part of the AI landscape, enabling various AI applications such as chatbots, language translation, and text generation.

In summary, the relationship between AI and LLMs is one of LLMs being a fundamental component of AI, specifically in the area of natural language processing and generation, and serving as a foundation model for various generative AI applications. (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Large_language_model, https://www.ibm.com/topics/artificial-intelligence)
